WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.620
Tesla's fleet GNSS correction turns isolated cars into a shared reference network that pins urban positioning back to the road for FSD. This is Tesla Shorts Time, Episode 558. A single vehicle in a glass canyon receives distorted satellite signals that drift its calculated position toward curbs or buildings. One car matches visible landmarks to a stored visual map and sends both its map pose and raw satellite measurements

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:59.520
to a server. Nearby vehicles receive the paired data, combine it with their own readings, and use real-time kinematic processing to calculate relative position vectors that correct the drift. The updated pose returns through the server to surrounding cars, giving the fleet a stronger shared reference. This approach moves FSD positioning from isolated receivers to a moving network that improves accuracy at city scale, without requiring direct line of sight

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:16.600
between vehicles. The method lowers per car hardware requirements while improving worst-case urban accuracy that regulators will scrutinize. While the positioning network strengthens the software stack, a separate regulatory probe is now testing the hardware side of the existing fleet.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:37.760
Regulators opened an investigation covering 1.2 million Tesla vehicles for potential suspension defects. The probe adds to existing legal and reputational pressure on the company. No specific defect description or recall scope has been released yet, but the scale of the fleet under review creates a new compliance workload.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:56.660
The development arrives while the stock trades lower on the day. Tesla will need to allocate engineering and legal resources to respond while production and software programs continue. Manufacturing pressure is also visible at the Texas plant, where a supplier dispute has slowed cyber truck output.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:12.020
A supplier is reportedly withholding tooling and demanding daily payments before releasing parts needed for cyber truck assembly. The dispute has slowed production at the Texas factory and forced Tesla to seek alternative sourcing or legal remedies.

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:20.660
The situation highlights supply chain leverage points that remain outside Tesla's direct control even after vertical integration efforts.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:32.160
Production targets for the vehicle face renewed pressure until the conflict resolves. Tesla is simultaneously investing ahead of production with new optimist thermal engineering roles.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:42.340
Tesla is actively recruiting thermal design and validation engineers in Palo Alto to address heat build-up in optimist actuators and power electronics.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:52.300
Human-sized limbs leave almost no room for conventional heat sinks, while continuous dynamic loads from walking and lifting generate non-stop heat.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:03:06.180
Standard air cooling falls short, pushing the team toward vapor chambers, two-phase cooling and advanced interface materials with dino testing required to validate custom joint actuators under extreme duty cycles.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:16.180
Quiet active cooling fans are mandatory for home and workplace use. The effort targets one of the core physical limits on robot runtime and performance.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:32.580
On the energy side of the business, Tesla is locking in long-term renewable supply instead of hardware constraints. Concord new energy signed three long-term power purchase agreements to supply electricity to Tesla operations in the United States.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:47.280
The deals add renewable generation capacity that supports both vehicle manufacturing and energy storage deployments. Tesla energy continues to secure dedicated supply contracts that reduce exposure to grid price volatility.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:04:02.520
The agreements expand the non-automotive revenue-based tied to utility scale projects. Tesla entered a long-term agreement to purchase one terawatt hour of renewable electricity annually from contour global's US project.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:16.880
The contract supports manufacturing operations and aligns with broader energy procurement goals. Securing dedicated renewable supply at this scale reduces reliance on spot market pricing for large industrial loads.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:33.780
The deal adds another data point on how Tesla's energy needs now intersect directly with utility scale generation. Tesla began offering GROC AI access to Indian users and opened test drives for the Model Y premium rear-wheel drive variant.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:46.840
The moves expand both software features and vehicle availability in a new market. Local customers can now experience the updated infotainment integration alongside the refreshed power train option.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:05:00.440
The rollout follows earlier regulatory approvals for vehicle sales in the country. Tesla opened customer test drives for the Model Y premium rear-wheel drive in India following earlier regulatory clearances.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:13.820
The variant offers a lower entry price point than the all-wheel drive versions already on sale. Local interest centers on range, charging access and software features in a market with growing EV incentives.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:21.260
The test drive program provides direct feedback on how the vehicle performs in Indian traffic and climate conditions.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:34.060
Tesla has met an additional performance milestone tied to Elon Musk's compensation plan. The package requires sustained market capitalization and operational targets across multiple years.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:47.860
Reaching this particular goal narrows the remaining hurdles but still leaves several others outstanding. Shareholders approved the structure years ago and each verified milestone reduces uncertainty around the final payout.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:06:04.640
The compensation structure remains one of the largest equity awards in public company history. Updated FSD safety data from five EU countries shows the system operating 5.2 times safer than manual driving across 65 million kilometers.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:18.460
The figures cover supervised operation on public roads in multiple regulatory environments. US drivers can use the European data set as an additional benchmark while awaiting domestic unsupervised approval.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:24.960
The release provides a concrete safety multiple that regulators on both sides of the Atlantic can reference.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:35.720
A recent video test compared reaction times across V14 light, V12.6.4 and V14.3 on the same scenarios.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:43.800
The comparison isolates measurable differences in how quickly each version responds to sudden obstacles or changing road conditions.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:57.200
The results provide a concrete data point on iteration speed within the current supervised stack. Tesla states that FSD V14 light improves proactive and reactive responsiveness.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:14.660
Now, one thing worth watching is how Tesla manages the new suspension inquiry. Regulators open a new probe covering 1.2 million vehicles for potential suspension defects, adding compliance and legal exposure at a time when the stock is already under pressure.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:23.180
The investigation expands the list of active regulatory matters without yet specifying defect details or recall scope.

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:37.500
How the company manages the inquiry will determine whether it stays contained or triggers broader scrutiny. Fleet level sensor fusion changes the unit economics of perception in a way single vehicle systems cannot match.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:54.100
When one car's visual map pose and raw GNSS measurements travel to a server and return corrected by relative vectors from nearby vehicles, the cost of accuracy spreads across the entire local fleet instead of remaining locked inside each machine.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:08:04.720
That shift matters because urban GNSS errors are not random noise but repeatable geometry created by the same buildings and atmospheric conditions every day.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:14.160
A network that measures those errors collectively reduces the per car compute and sensor burden required to stay inside a lane at highway speed.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:29.240
The practical consequence appears first in dense corridors where individual fixes fail most often. A vehicle entering an intersection can inherit a sharper pose from cars already crossing it, even without direct camera overlap.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:42.240
This matters for FSD because regulatory approval for unsupervised operation will likely hinge on demonstrated performance under the worst local conditions rather than average conditions across a continent.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:57.720
The fleet approach supplies exactly that local calibration at marginal extra cost once the server and map infrastructure exist. For the business, the same architecture lowers the hardware specification needed inside each new vehicle.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:10.320
If relative positioning from the group can compensate for some individual sensor drift, the company can delay or reduce the scope of next generation onboard compute while still meeting safety targets.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:21.400
That option directly affects capital intensity and gross margin on the vehicle side, an outcome that matters more than any single software release when production volume scale.

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:30.820
The open question is how quickly regulators accept fleet derived corrections as equivalent to independent sensing when liability questions arise.

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:40.320
Before we go, the Optimus thermal engineering push will show whether vapor chamber solutions can keep pace with continuous walking loads in the coming months.

